      "instance_name": "undocumented_migration",
      "label": "Undocumented Migration",
      "description": "The meme references the real-world phenomenon of undocumented migration, particularly from Mexico to the United States. This involves individuals crossing borders without legal authorization, often through dangerous routes. The meme uses this concept to frame the visual of the men as a stereotypical representation of undocumented migrants, reinforcing negative perceptions.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_668acc60"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_03f0c879",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "mexican_immigration_stereotype",
      "label": "Mexican Immigration Stereotype",
      "description": "A specific stereotype that portrays Mexican immigrants as inherently criminal, lazy, or dangerous, often associated with illegal border crossing. This stereotype is perpetuated in media, politics, and popular culture, and is used to justify restrictive immigration policies and xenophobic attitudes. The meme 'mexicans road trip' is a direct example of this harmful trope.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_668acc60"
      },
